//! Parity of the single-objective acquisition functions of phase 8 with
//! BoTorch (fixtures in `tests/fixtures/phase8_so_acquisition/*.json`,
//! generated by `scripts/generate_fixtures.py --phase 8-so-acquisition`
//! against BoTorch main, with BoTorch's random numbers recorded):
//!
//! * qKnowledgeGradient (posterior mean, `current_value`, pending points,
//!   posterior transforms, linear MC objectives) and
//!   qMultiFidelityKnowledgeGradient (projection, trace observations, cost);
//! * qNoisyExpectedImprovement (`cache_root` on and off, pending points),
//!   qLowerConfidenceBound, qPosteriorStandardDeviation;
//! * (Log)NoisyExpectedImprovement, LogProbabilityOfFeasibility,
//!   ScalarizedPosteriorMean, qAnalyticProbabilityOfImprovement;
//! * the max-value entropy search family (BoTorch's max values);
//! * `get_optimal_samples`, qJointEntropySearch, qPredictiveEntropySearch,
//!   PathwiseThompsonSampling, qNegIntegratedPosteriorVariance;
//! * the penalties and wrappers;
//! * `optimize_acqf` of qKG and GIBBON from BoTorch's initial conditions.
//!
//! Tolerances: values 1e-9, gradients 1e-8 (relative to the largest
//! component, entries within 1e-14 count as equal). Where BoTorch's gradients
//! are wrong (qKG with an MC objective, meta-pytorch/botorch#3427), the
//! gradients are compared with central differences (1e-6 relative: step
//! 1e-6). `get_optimal_samples`: 1e-6 (L-BFGS-B). `optimize_acqf`: all but
//! one restart reach BoTorch's value within 1e-6, with candidates within
//! 1e-3. Run with `--nocapture` to print the error tables.

